{"id": "q004", "question": "Is there a way for us to write code that would execute after the fastapi app starts?", "expected_pages": ["advanced/events.md"], "hit_rank": 1, "top_pages": ["advanced/events.md", "tutorial/testing.md", "tutorial/first-steps.md", "index.md", "deployment/docker.md"], "result": {"answer": "The excerpts don't describe code that runs after the app has fully started. The closest option is the `startup` event, which runs before the app starts receiving requests:\n\n```python\n@app.on_event(\"startup\")\nasync def startup_event():\n    items[\"foo\"] = {\"name\": \"Fighters\"}\n    items[\"bar\"] = {\"name\": \"Tenders\"}\n```\n\nYou can add more than one startup handler, and the app won't receive requests until all of them complete [1]. This section is titled \"Alternative Events (deprecated)\" [1].", "citations": [{"number": 1, "heading_path": "Lifespan Events > Alternative Events (deprecated) > `startup` event", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/events/#startup-event", "page_path": "advanced/events.md"}], "found": true, "retrieved": [{"id": "advanced/events.md#startup-event", "page_path": "advanced/events.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/events/#startup-event", "similarity": 0.5905}, {"id": "tutorial/testing.md#fastapi-app-file", "page_path": "tutorial/testing.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/testing/#fastapi-app-file", "similarity": 0.5804}, {"id": "tutorial/first-steps.md#first-steps", "page_path": "tutorial/first-steps.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/first-steps/#first-steps", "similarity": 0.5767}, {"id": "index.md#run-it", "page_path": "index.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/#run-it", "similarity": 0.5751}, {"id": "deployment/docker.md#create-the-fastapi-code", "page_path": "deployment/docker.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/deployment/docker/#create-the-fastapi-code", "similarity": 0.5721}, {"id": "tutorial/first-steps.md#recap", "page_path": "tutorial/first-steps.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/first-steps/#recap", "similarity": 0.5668}], "usage": {"embedding_tokens": 19, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "input_tokens": 2542, "output_tokens": 552}, "latency_ms": {"retrieval": 346, "llm": 3069, "total": 3415}}}
{"id": "q005", "question": "How to make BackgroundTasks manager?", "expected_pages": ["tutorial/request-files.md", "tutorial/background-tasks.md"], "hit_rank": 1, "top_pages": ["tutorial/background-tasks.md", "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "reference/background.md"], "result": {"answer": "The docs don't describe creating a `BackgroundTasks` object yourself. Instead, you declare it as a parameter and FastAPI creates it for you: \"FastAPI will create the object of type `BackgroundTasks` for you and pass it as that parameter.\" [3]\n\nTo use it:\n\n1. Import `BackgroundTasks` from `fastapi` and declare a parameter typed as `BackgroundTasks` in your *path operation function* (or a dependency) [1][3][5].\n2. Call `.add_task()` on that object, passing the task function, its positional arguments, and any keyword arguments [6].\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import BackgroundTasks, FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\ndef write_notification(email: str, message=\"\"):\n    with open(\"log.txt\", mode=\"w\") as email_file:\n        content = f\"notification for {email}: {message}\"\n        email_file.write(content)\n\n@app.post(\"/send-notification/{email}\")\nasync def send_notification(email: str, background_tasks: BackgroundTasks):\n    background_tasks.add_task(write_notification, email, message=\"some notification\")\n    return {\"message\": \"Notification sent in the background\"}\n```\n[3][6]\n\nThe docs also note that `BackgroundTasks` is meant for small tasks that need access to the same app's variables and objects. For heavy computation that doesn't need to share memory, they suggest tools like Celery [4].", "citations": [{"number": 1, "heading_path": "Background Tasks > Recap", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#recap", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md"}, {"number": 3, "heading_path": "Background Tasks > Using `BackgroundTasks`", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#using-backgroundtasks", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md"}, {"number": 4, "heading_path": "Background Tasks > Caveat", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#caveat", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md"}, {"number": 5, "heading_path": "Background Tasks - `BackgroundTasks`", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/reference/background/", "page_path": "reference/background.md"}, {"number": 6, "heading_path": "Background Tasks > Add the background task", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#add-the-background-task", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md"}], "found": true, "retrieved": [{"id": "tutorial/background-tasks.md#recap", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#recap", "similarity": 0.5878}, {"id": "tutorial/background-tasks.md#technical-details", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#technical-details", "similarity": 0.5428}, {"id": "tutorial/background-tasks.md#using-backgroundtasks", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#using-backgroundtasks", "similarity": 0.5382}, {"id": "tutorial/background-tasks.md#caveat", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#caveat", "similarity": 0.5095}, {"id": "reference/background.md#", "page_path": "reference/background.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/reference/background/", "similarity": 0.5087}, {"id": "tutorial/background-tasks.md#add-the-background-task", "page_path": "tutorial/background-tasks.md", "url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/background-tasks/#add-the-background-task", "similarity": 0.5012}], "usage": {"embedding_tokens": 7, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "input_tokens": 1801, "output_tokens": 816}, "latency_ms": {"retrieval": 32